WEBVTT

00:01:59.448 --> 00:02:01.826
access to mental health care
in these communities

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.619
is virtually non-existent.

00:02:04.787 --> 00:02:06.747
So just to give you an idea,

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:07.957
in the United States,

00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:10.418
there are about 270
mental health care workers

00:02:10.418 --> 00:02:12.295
for every 100,000 people.

00:02:13.296 --> 00:02:15.506
In Honduras, this drops to two.

00:02:16.549 --> 00:02:18.968
So we're left with this classic conundrum.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.845
We know how to help solve the problem,

00:02:20.845 --> 00:02:22.847
but we don't have the resources to do it.

00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:28.394
But what if we re-envision what
or who these resources could be?

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.189
I think we should,